---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Manuel Valle Torre - Learning Analytics"
  description="PhD Student in Learning Analytics at TU Delft"
>
  <Header slot="header" />
  
  <main class="space-y-12">
    <section class="flex items-center gap-8">
      <div class="w-24 h-24 rounded-full bg-gray-200 dark:bg-gray-700 flex-shrink-0">
        <!-- Placeholder for profile picture. Replace with <Image /> component when ready -->
        <!-- Example: <Image src={profilePic} alt="Manuel Valle Torre" class="rounded-full" /> -->
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-2">
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">Manuel Valle Torre</h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
          PhD Candidate in Learning Analytics at TU Delft, exploring how data and AI can enhance education.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
      <p>
        I'm fascinated by emerging technologies and their potential to reshape how we learn. 
        As a researcher at the <a href="https://www.educationandlearning.nl/home">Centre for Education and Learning (CEL)</a>, 
        I focus on using Learning Analytics to understand and improve educational processes, particularly with the rise of Generative AI.
      </p>
      <p>
        My work involves analyzing how students interact with Large Language Models (LLMs) to uncover patterns that can inform the design of better learning tools.
        This research led me to create <a href="/reports/jelai">JELAI</a>, a Jupyter-based environment for studying these interactions.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before my PhD, I was a Research Engineer at the Web Information Systems group at TU Delft. Outside of academia, I enjoy music, cooking, and making my own <a href="/sauces">hot sauces</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Feel free to explore my <a href="/publications">publications</a> or reach out if you'd like to connect.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-white/70 dark:bg-gray-900/60 shadow-sm p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-4">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 text-sm text-accent">
        <span class="px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-accent/10 text-accent dark:text-accent-dark">Interactive</span>
        <span class="px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-accent/10 text-accent dark:text-accent-dark">GenAI</span>
        <span class="px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-accent/10 text-accent dark:text-accent-dark">Learning Analytics</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Latest report: AI in Education – The Missing Link</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
        I’ve been experimenting with narrative data stories. This interactive walk-through explains why deploying
        Generative AI without a Learning Analytics feedback loop leaves educators flying blind. Explore the risks,
        the dual feedback model, and actionable recommendations.
      </p>
      <a
        href="/reports/ai-in-education/"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-medium text-accent hover:text-accent-dark transition-colors"
      >
        Read the interactive report
        <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>